hole-tolerance-residue: old-engine (6.87/7.01/7.24) bolt holes from the group's own tolerance field (any sign / size), no holes in non-plies
Base: DB1 kit code i == code j for db1bolts.py (md5 0f67b818e002eed7e108a5948a08a5f1) and db1step.py (md5 6039ca91db4ec428884cab6947528d80).
Apply in the kit dir:  patch -p0 < hole_tolerance_residue.patch   -> db1bolts.py md5 079ffea6d105142ff41e8d2a9340c8aa, db1step.py md5 72029bbf4e7f3b1c0048379843a2e249
Then bump worker.py CODE (e.g. z3-db1-2026-10-01k) so redo() re-runs every model of older code (best-of keeps the better STEP).
Changes:
  * db1bolts.tolerance_status(): field 4 of MM<d>*<L>/<slot x>/<slot y>/<tol>/... used as stored when the string has the 11-field layout:
      t = 0 -> hole = d, t < 0 -> hole < d, t > 10 -> oversize anchor holes; d + t <= 0 -> no hole (STUD groups); hole > 4d -> still nominal.
    Codes e-j accepted only 0 < t <= 10, so genuine 0 / negative / > 10 values were cut at d + ISO 273 / AISC clearance (hole_clearance_nominal).
  * bolts_of(): bolt dicts carry tol_status and slot (slot x, slot y)
  * catalog_geometry(): skip {'ambiguous': n} head entries of bolt_catalog.json (code i/j raise KeyError 's' -> convert_error on 3 models)
  * db1step.convert_old(): no cut when the hole diameter <= 0; no cut in a member the bolt is not a ply of: member material over the whole
    shank +- 2d (bolt running inside a rod / block / beam), or a member parallel to the bolt whose material reaches past an end of that
    window (rods / bars threaded through the hole). Code i bored ROD48/ROD50 bars along their axis; the true 60/70 mm holes would sever
    them. Contour plates bolted through their thickness and thin parts along the axis (modelled washers / nuts) are cut as before. bolt_stats gains holes_by_diameter_source, holes_not_cut_zero_diameter, holes_not_cut_bolt_inside_part,
    bolt_inside_part_why/_profiles, holes_in_slotted_groups_cut_round. holes_nominal_clearance keeps its meaning (build_index.py standin).
